<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Calculate Your Tip Quickly</h2>
    <p>Using our gratuity tool takes all the guesswork and mental math out of paying your restaurant tab. You begin by entering your exact bill amount into the topmost box. From there you can simply tap on one of our most popular percentage buttons which represent standard tipping rates. If the service was particularly exceptional or if you want to leave a very specific amount you can type your preferred percentage into the custom box.</p>
    <p>If you are dining out with friends or colleagues the final step is incredibly helpful safely splitting the financial burden. Just enter the number of people sitting at your table. Our system immediately updates the bottom section calculating the exact tip amount the total combined bill and exactly how much cash each person needs to contribute. The numbers change live as you type so you never have to hit a recalculate button.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>The Standard Tipping Formula</h2>
    <p>Calculating gratuity manually is a simple mathematical equation taking your total charge and multiplying it by a decimal percentage. For example if you want to leave a standard twenty percent tip on a fifty dollar bill you multiply fifty by zero point two zero. This gives you a ten dollar tip making your grand total sixty dollars.</p>
    <p>The formula for splitting the check is also straightforward. You simply take that grand total and divide it by the number of paying guests. If three people are splitting that sixty dollar total the math divides it evenly into twenty dollars per person. Our tool strictly follows these exact financial equations while ensuring that no rounding errors occur giving you a flawless breakdown every single time you dine out.</p>
</section>

<section class="examples">
    <h2>Common Tipping Examples</h2>
    <p>Let us look at a few realistic examples of what you might encounter when dealing with different service industries.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Standard Restaurant Dinner:</strong> A typical seventy five dollar dinner bill normally receives a twenty percent tip. The gratuity equals exactly fifteen dollars resulting in a total final payment of ninety dollars.</li>
        <li><strong>Hair Salon or Barber:</strong> If your haircut costs forty dollars standard practice is to leave an eighteen percent tip. This amounts to seven dollars and twenty cents making your final checkout forty seven dollars and twenty cents.</li>
        <li><strong>Coffee Shop:</strong> A simple espresso charge of four dollars usually receives a small fifteen percent gratuity. The resulting tip is sixty cents.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

