<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    
    <h3>Should I tip based on the pre tax or post tax bill amount?</h3>
    <p>General etiquette suggests calculating your gratuity based upon the pre tax subtotal of your meal. Tipping on the final post tax amount means you are unnecessarily tipping on government surcharges. However many generous patrons simply tip on the final total because it is much faster and easier to read right off the receipt.</p>
    
    <h3>What is the standard tipping rate right now?</h3>
    <p>In most North American restaurants twenty percent has firmly become the standard baseline for average to good service. Leaving eighteen percent generally signifies adequate but unimpressive service. Leaving fifteen percent or less usually communicates active dissatisfaction with your dining experience.</p>
    
    <h3>Does this calculator round the split amounts for uneven groups?</h3>
    <p>Yes our tool intelligently rounds the per person amounts to the nearest penny ensuring the physical cash split remains accurate and completely practical. You will never see a fraction of a cent displayed.</p>
</section>

